      ["Which is right for a city?",["à Paris","en Paris","au Paris","aux Paris"],0,"Cities take plain ‹à›: ‹à Paris›."],
      ["What does ‹à› + ‹le› become?",["à le","au","aux","du"],1,"‹à› + ‹le› always contracts to ‹au›."],
      ["How do you say in Japan (‹le Japon› is masculine)?",["en Japon","à Japon","au Japon","aux Japon"],2,"A masculine country takes ‹au›: ‹au Japon›."]
